{
  "_comment": [
    "Canonical server responses for the admin API — ONE file, read by BOTH sides.",
    "",
    "Defect 9 is why this exists. The Dart client read `parity.unpaired` as a list",
    "and called .length on it; the server has always sent a count. `7 as List?`",
    "threw, and because the Operations screen loads four sources with Future.wait,",
    "that one cast killed the entire screen for the operator. Every test in the repo",
    "stayed green: they checked that the endpoint had a caller, never that the two",
    "sides agreed about the SHAPE of what crosses the wire.",
    "",
    "The contract is checked from both ends against these samples:",
    "  - src/lib/__tests__/adminContract.test.ts asserts the SERVER's declared",
    "    types still match the types recorded here (a field that changes from",
    "    number to array fails there);",
    "  - admin_flutter/test/contract_test.dart feeds each sample through the real",
    "    fromJson and asserts it parses (a client that expects the wrong type",
    "    fails there).",
    "",
    "Values are representative, not real. Shapes are the point."
  ],

